[{"n":1,"title":"The Stone Roses","artist":"The Stone Roses","year":1989,"mbid":"88b86fe0-26f5-3949-817a-8082145e704d","heard":true,"cover":"https://dn721807.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-966d143c-d0f4-46fc-a265-e7394b04a7b9/mbid-966d143c-d0f4-46fc-a265-e7394b04a7b9-28642859817.png","spotify_id":null,"spotify_url":null,"desc_lfm_album":"The Stone Roses LP was recorded between June 1988 and Febuary 1989 by the Stone Roses with producer John Leckie. It was then released on the 13th of March 1989 on the Silvertone music label. The artwork for the album was inspired by American artist Jackson Pollock. The album was then released in the United States on the 2nd of May 1989, following a release in Australia in December that year. The album has since seen various re-releases, in September 1991, then in 1999 for the 10 year anniversary edition and just recently it was announced their would be a .","desc_lfm_artist":"The Stone Roses was an English rock band formed in Manchester in 1983. They were one of the pioneering groups of the Madchester movement in the late 1980s and early 1990s. The band's classic and most prominent lineup consisted of vocalist Ian Brown, guitarist John Squire, bassist Mani, and drummer Reni.\n\nThe Stone Roses released their eponymous debut album in 1989. The album was a breakthrough success for the band, receiving widespread critical acclaim, and is regarded by many as one of the greatest British albums ever recorded.","desc_mb_album":null,"desc_mb_artist":null,"yt_id":"P_9PU0Si4b0","genres":["psychedelic","indie rock","neo-psychedelia","jangle pop","britpop","c86"],"rym":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/the-stone-roses/the-stone-roses/","scaruffi_rating":null,"scaruffi_note":null,"wikipedia_url":null,"aoty_user_score":86,"aoty_critic_score":82,"metacritic_score":null,"label":null},{"n":2,"title":"Technique","artist":"New Order","year":1989,"mbid":"a0902fc4-e3d9-3b2b-bc94-cd4d0e59db29","heard":true,"cover":"https://dn710905.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-01681b1d-3068-3689-b879-efefde1f7b3b/mbid-01681b1d-3068-3689-b879-efefde1f7b3b-2546509254.jpg","spotify_id":null,"spotify_url":null,"desc_lfm_album":"Technique is the fifth studio album by English rock band New Order. Released on 30 January 1989 by Factory Records, the album was partly recorded on the island of Ibiza, and incorporates Balearic beat and acid house influences into the group's dance-rock sound. The album was influenced by the then growing acid scene, and Sumner's experiences at Shoom in London. It was also New Order's final studio album to be released under Factory Records (though not their final Factory release, that being the following year's \"World in Motion\"); the label would declare bankruptcy in 1992 following a severe financial downturn .","desc_lfm_artist":"New Order is an English new wave/synthpop band which formed in 1980 in Salford, England, United Kingdom by the three remaining members of Joy Division. The band's classic lineup consists of Bernard Sumner (vocals, guitar, keyboards), Peter Hook (bass, electronic percussion), Gillian Gilbert (keyboards, guitar) and Stephen Morris (drums, keyboards). The group effectively disbanded in 1993 but reformed in 1998. Gilbert left in 2001 to look after her and Morris' children and was replaced by guitarist/keyboardist Phil Cunningham.","desc_mb_album":null,"desc_mb_artist":null,"yt_id":"QBziNQAm85U","genres":["new wave","synth-pop","alternative dance","dance-rock"],"rym":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/new-order/technique","scaruffi_rating":null,"scaruffi_note":null,"wikipedia_url":null,"aoty_user_score":81,"aoty_critic_score":77,"metacritic_score":null,"label":null},{"n":3,"title":"Pills ’n’ Thrills and Bellyaches","artist":"Happy Mondays","year":1990,"mbid":"f63a7c53-571f-3d4a-a942-053f56590605","heard":false,"cover":"https://dn710901.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-99cba4e5-bda4-3c70-9734-acf296f7da3a/mbid-99cba4e5-bda4-3c70-9734-acf296f7da3a-4360036213.jpg","spotify_id":null,"spotify_url":null,"desc_lfm_album":null,"desc_lfm_artist":"Happy Mondays are an alternative rock band formed in Salford, Greater Manchester, U.K. in 1985, notable for being a forerunner of the immensely popular neo-psychedelic   indie-dance movement (known as 'madchester' for some groups) that mashed up funk, pop, rock, and other genres. Still touring to this day, the band is fronted by Shaun Ryder, who formed the band with his bass-playing brother Paul Ryder. The classic line-up for the rest of the band consisted of their friend Bez","desc_mb_album":"Two album cover were used. The original cover consisted of a montage of popular children's sweet wrappers. This was later changed following objections from the U.S. manufacturers.","desc_mb_artist":"Legend has it that Factory Records boss Tony Wilson signed the band after seeing them finish last in a battle of the bands competition at his The Hacienda night club.","yt_id":"0pQXW1JozXY","genres":["alternative rock","indie rock","leftfield","neo-psychedelia","alternative dance"],"rym":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/happy-mondays/pills-n-thrills-and-bellyaches","scaruffi_rating":null,"scaruffi_note":null,"wikipedia_url":null,"aoty_user_score":null,"aoty_critic_score":null,"metacritic_score":null,"label":null},{"n":4,"title":"90","artist":"808 State","year":2090,"mbid":null,"heard":false,"cover":"","spotify_id":null,"spotify_url":null,"desc_lfm_album":null,"desc_lfm_artist":null,"desc_mb_album":null,"desc_mb_artist":null,"yt_id":"3xVPwp5CkXA","genres":[],"rym":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/808-state/90","scaruffi_rating":null,"scaruffi_note":null,"wikipedia_url":null,"aoty_user_score":null,"aoty_critic_score":null,"metacritic_score":null,"label":null},{"n":5,"title":"Ex:el","artist":"808 State","year":1991,"mbid":"802b0c50-ef1e-3c15-a830-7ed468f0565e","heard":false,"cover":"https://dn721604.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-ec3c0a17-780c-485d-a65d-feb49228b6d2/mbid-ec3c0a17-780c-485d-a65d-feb49228b6d2-29165255724.jpg","spotify_id":null,"spotify_url":"https://open.spotify.com/album/5q3FCcPTqLUT0UkrqMb45z","desc_lfm_album":"ex:el is the third studio album by 808 State, released on 4 March 1991 by ZTT Records. In contrast to the band's previous work, the album features more catchy melodies and heavier acid techno beats and percussion, \"embracing earlier flirtations with hip-hop and industrial music\". The album also features the guest vocals of Bernard Sumner of Joy Division and New Order, who sings on \"Spanish Heart\". In addition, Björk sings on \"Qmart\" and \"Ooops\", and is credited with co-writing both; this album marked the start of a long-running working relationship between Björk and Graham Massey. It is considered to be .","desc_lfm_artist":"808 State are an electronic music outfit formed in 1988 in Manchester, England taking their name from the Roland TR-808 drum machine. Widely regarded as one of the pioneers of acid house, they were formed by Graham Massey (from ex-Factory Records band Biting Tongues), Martin Price and Gerald Simpson (later to record as A Guy Called Gerald).\n\nThey released their debut Newbuild in 1988. Autechre and Aphex Twin have often cited the album as being enormously influential","desc_mb_album":null,"desc_mb_artist":null,"yt_id":"a5jLI8J0aRU","genres":["leftfield","techno"],"rym":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/808-state/ex_el","scaruffi_rating":7.0,"scaruffi_note":null,"wikipedia_url":null,"aoty_user_score":null,"aoty_critic_score":null,"metacritic_score":null,"label":null},{"n":6,"title":"Between 10th and 11th","artist":"The Charlatans UK","year":1992,"mbid":null,"heard":false,"cover":"","spotify_id":null,"spotify_url":null,"desc_lfm_album":null,"desc_lfm_artist":null,"desc_mb_album":null,"desc_mb_artist":null,"yt_id":"xivKBrdgz3c","genres":[],"rym":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/the-charlatans-uk/between-10th-and-11th","scaruffi_rating":null,"scaruffi_note":null,"wikipedia_url":null,"aoty_user_score":null,"aoty_cri